# Environment Configuration for Firebase Integration

## 🔥 Firebase Configuration Variables

# Firebase Project Configuration
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=trueworkers-dev
FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY='{"type":"service_account","project_id":"trueworkers-dev","private_key_id":"","private_key":"","client_email":"","client_id":"","auth_uri":"https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/auth","token_uri":"https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token","auth_provider_x509_cert_url":"https://www.googleapis.com/oauth2/v1/certs","client_x509_cert_url":""}'

# Database Configuration (Existing)
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_PORT=5432
DB_USERNAME=mesteri_user
DB_PASSWORD=mesteri_pass
DB_DATABASE=mesteri_db
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://mesteri_user:mesteri_pass@localhost:5432/mesteri_db?schema=public"

# App Configuration (Existing)
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3000

# Prisma Configuration (Existing)
PRISMA_GENERATE_DATAPROXY=false
PRISMA_GENERATE_ENGINE_TYPE="library"

# WebSocket Configuration (Existing)
WS_CORS_ORIGIN="http://localhost:3000"

## 🚨 IMPORTANT SETUP INSTRUCTIONS

1. Replace FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY with actual service account JSON (as single line)
2. Update FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID to match your Firebase project
3. Download service account key from Firebase Console:
   - Go to Project Settings → Service Accounts
   - Click "Generate new private key"
   - Copy JSON content and minify to single line
   - Replace the placeholder value above

## 📱 Flutter Configuration

After setting up Firebase projects, you'll need to:
1. Download google-services.json for each app
2. Place in appropriate Flutter app directories:
   - app_client/android/app/google-services.json
   - app_mester/android/app/google-services.json

## 🔄 Environment-Specific Files

- Development: Use trueworkers-dev project
- Staging: Use trueworkers-staging project  
- Production: Use trueworkers-prod project